APX.si = {"country":{"name":"Slovenia","tagline":"A small country with three wine worlds: Collio's mirror in Brda, the bora-swept Karst, and the steep Styrian hills where the world's oldest vine still fruits.","classification":"Slovenia's quality categories (ZGP, *vino z zaščitenim geografskim poreklom*: PDO wine) are tied to its nine wine districts, each a PDO: Goriška Brda, Vipavska dolina, Kras and Slovenska Istra in Primorska; Štajerska Slovenija and Prekmurje in Podravje; Bizeljsko Sremič, Dolenjska and Bela krajina in Posavje. Within PDO wine a label may say *kakovostno vino ZGP* (quality wine) or *vrhunsko vino ZGP* (premium wine, tasting-scored and stricter), and the Prädikat-style terms *pozna trgatev* (late harvest), *izbor*, *jagodni izbor*, *suhi jagodni izbor* and *ledeno vino* apply to sweet wines. Five wines have special status as PTP (*priznano tradicionalno poimenovanje*, recognised traditional designation), each also an EU PDO: Teran (Refošk from the Karst), Cviček (Dolenjska), Metliška črnina and Belokranjec (Bela krajina) and Bizeljčan (Bizeljsko Sremič). A new Wine Act was adopted as a government bill in November 2025 and was in parliament during 2026."},"regions":[{"name":"Primorska","slug":"primorska","tagline":"Collio's other half, the bora-blasted Vipava valley, the red earth of the Karst and the Istrian coast.","ids":["si-goriska-brda","si-kras","si-slovenska-istra","si-teran","si-vipavska-dolina"]},{"name":"Podravje","slug":"podravje","tagline":"Steep Styrian terraces and Pannonian plains: crisp aromatic whites, Šipon and the world's oldest vine.","ids":["si-prekmurje","si-stajerska-slovenija"]},{"name":"Posavje","slug":"posavje","tagline":"The Sava and Krka hills of zidanice cottages, tart Cviček and the sand caves of Bizeljsko.","ids":["si-bela-krajina","si-belokranjec","si-bizeljsko-sremic","si-bizeljcan","si-cvicek","si-dolenjska","si-metliska-crnina"]}],"items":{"si-bela-krajina":{"name":"Bela krajina","cat":"ZGP","region":"Posavje","created":"EU PDO 2006","area_ha":300,"styles":["red","white","sweet"],"grapes":"Modra frankinja, Žametovka, Laški rizling, Kraljevina, Rumeni muškat","summary":"Bela krajina ('White March'), named for its birch trees and white linen dress, is a small district (about 300 ha) on the Kolpa river by the Croatian border around Metlika, Semič and Črnomelj. It makes Metliška črnina, Belokranjec, Modra frankinja and some of Slovenia's best ice wines and botrytised sweet wines.","rslug":"posavje"},"si-belokranjec":{"name":"Belokranjec","cat":"PTP","region":"Posavje","created":"EU PDO 2006","styles":["white"],"grapes":"Laški rizling, Kraljevina, Beli pinot, Chardonnay, Rumeni muškat, Zeleni silvanec, Renski rizling","summary":"Belokranjec is the white partner of Metliška črnina: a fresh, fragrant white blend from Bela krajina based on Laški rizling, Kraljevina, Beli pinot, Rumeni muškat and Zeleni silvanec. Its amended specification was approved in March 2026.","rslug":"posavje"},"si-bizeljcan":{"name":"Bizeljčan","cat":"PTP","region":"Posavje","created":"EU PDO 2009","styles":["white","red"],"grapes":"White: Laški rizling, Rumeni plavec, Ranfol; red: Modra frankinja, Žametovka, Portugalka","summary":"Bizeljčan is the recognised traditional designation of Bizeljsko Sremič, made as a white blend (Laški rizling, Rumeni plavec, Ranfol, Kraljevina and others) and as a red (Modra frankinja, Žametovka, Portugalka). Both are light, fresh, everyday wines.","rslug":"posavje"},"si-bizeljsko-sremic":{"name":"Bizeljsko Sremič","cat":"ZGP","region":"Posavje","created":"EU PDO 2006","area_ha":700,"styles":["white","red","sparkling","sweet"],"grapes":"Laški rizling, Rumeni plavec, Ranfol, Kraljevina, Modra frankinja, Žametovka","summary":"Bizeljsko Sremič lies in the far east of Posavje by the Croatian border, about 700 ha. Quartz sand under the vineyards let growers dig *repnice*, caves originally for storing turnips (*repa*) that now age wine at a steady temperature. The district makes Bizeljčan blends, sweet wines and traditional-method sparkling (Istenič is the best-known house).","producers":["Istenič","Najger"],"rslug":"posavje"},"si-cvicek":{"name":"Cviček","cat":"PTP","region":"Posavje","created":"EU PDO 2006","styles":["rose","red"],"grapes":"Žametovka, Modra frankinja, Kraljevina, Laški rizling, Rumeni plavec","summary":"Cviček is a recognised traditional designation for a light, pale red wine from Dolenjska made by blending red and white grapes: mainly Žametovka and Modra frankinja with Kraljevina, Laški rizling and others. It is low in alcohol (typically 8.5 to 10%) and high in acidity, drunk young and cool. Slovenia's ministry approved an amended specification for Cviček in September 2025.","nerd_note":"Cviček is one of the few protected wines in the EU that must blend red and white grapes; its low alcohol made it a 'doctor's wine' recommended to convalescents.","rslug":"posavje"},"si-dolenjska":{"name":"Dolenjska","cat":"ZGP","region":"Posavje","created":"EU PDO 2006","area_ha":1350,"styles":["red","rose","white"],"grapes":"Žametovka, Modra frankinja, Kraljevina, Laški rizling, Rumeni plavec","summary":"Dolenjska is the hilly heart of Posavje around Novo mesto and Trebnje, about 1,350 ha of small vineyards and *zidanice* cottages. It is best known for Cviček but also makes varietal Modra frankinja, Žametovka and whites from Kraljevina, Laški rizling and Rumeni plavec.","rslug":"posavje"},"si-goriska-brda":{"name":"Goriška Brda","cat":"ZGP","region":"Primorska","created":"EU PDO 2006","area_ha":1800,"styles":["white","orange","red","sparkling","sweet"],"grapes":"Rebula, Zeleni sauvignon (Friulano), Malvazija, Chardonnay, Sivi pinot, Sauvignon, Pikolit; Merlot, Cabernet, Pokalca","summary":"Goriška Brda ('Gorizia hills') is the Slovenian half of the Collio, a maze of flysch ridges and hilltop villages between the Soča and Idrija rivers on the Italian border, about 1,800 ha. Its signature grape is Rebula (Ribolla Gialla), which makes everything from crisp, citrusy whites to amber wines macerated for months on the skins. Zeleni sauvignon (Friulano), Malvazija, Chardonnay, Sivi pinot and the sweet Pikolit add range; Merlot and Cabernet thrive on the warmer slopes, and the local red Pokalca (Schioppettino) persists. The cooperative Klet Brda in Dobrovo is Slovenia's largest producer, but the district's name abroad comes from family estates: Movia, Klinec, Kabaj, Edi Simčič, Marjan Simčič, Ščurek, Erzetič, Dolfo, Štekar and Gašper.","terroir":"Eocene flysch (*opoka*): alternating marl and sandstone that weathers into well-drained, lime-rich soil; terraced slopes of 75 to 400 m; the Julian Alps block cold northern air and the Adriatic is 25 km away.","producers":["Movia","Klinec","Kabaj","Edi Simčič","Marjan Simčič","Ščurek","Štekar","Klet Brda","Erzetič","Dolfo"],"nerd_note":"Movia's Puro sparkling wine is sold undisgorged; the drinker opens it upside down under water (or into a bowl) to release the lees, a theatrical ritual devised by Aleš Kristančič.","rslug":"primorska"},"si-kras":{"name":"Kras","cat":"ZGP","region":"Primorska","created":"EU PDO 2006","area_ha":560,"styles":["red","white","orange"],"grapes":"Refošk (Teran), Vitovska, Malvazija, Sauvignon, Chardonnay","summary":"The Kras (Karst) is the limestone plateau behind Trieste, about 560 ha of vineyard in pockets of red earth between dolines, dry-stone walls and sumac. It is the home of Teran, the deep purple, high-acid wine of Refošk grown on terra rossa, and of Vitovska and Malvazija whites, often macerated. Families such as Čotar, Renčel, Lisjak and Štoka in villages like Tomaj, Dutovlje and Gorjansko age their wines in caves cut into the limestone.","terroir":"Iron-rich terra rossa in hollows of karst limestone, 200 to 400 m; thin soils, drought stress and the bora.","producers":["Čotar","Renčel","Lisjak","Štoka","Vinakras"],"nerd_note":"Kras growers often have to break the limestone with machines and import soil to plant a vineyard, which is why the district stays tiny.","rslug":"primorska"},"si-metliska-crnina":{"name":"Metliška črnina","cat":"PTP","region":"Posavje","created":"EU PDO 2009","styles":["red"],"grapes":"Modra frankinja, Žametovka, Portugalka, Šentlovrenka, Gamay, Modri pinot, Zweigelt","summary":"Metliška črnina ('black of Metlika') is Bela krajina's traditional red blend, dominated by Modra frankinja and Žametovka with Portugalka, Šentlovrenka, Gamay and others. It is deep coloured, dry, medium-bodied and fruity. The ministry approved an amended specification in March 2026.","rslug":"posavje"},"si-prekmurje":{"name":"Prekmurje","cat":"ZGP","region":"Podravje","created":"EU PDO 2006","area_ha":440,"styles":["white"],"grapes":"Laški rizling, Šipon, Sauvignon, Renski rizling, Beli pinot","summary":"Prekmurje is the flat-to-rolling Pannonian corner of Slovenia beyond the Mura, bordering Hungary and Austria, with about 440 ha in two hill groups: the Goričko hills and the Lendavske gorice. The wines are Laški rizling, Šipon, Sauvignon and Renski rizling, and the area has a strong Hungarian minority; Marof's Mačkovci winery has given the district international attention.","producers":["Marof","Cuk","Vino Kobal"],"rslug":"podravje"},"si-slovenska-istra":{"name":"Slovenska Istra","cat":"ZGP","region":"Primorska","created":"EU PDO 2009","area_ha":1850,"styles":["white","red","rose"],"grapes":"Malvazija, Refošk, Rumeni muškat, Cabernet Sauvignon, Merlot","summary":"Slovenska Istra covers the warm flysch hills behind the Slovenian coast at Koper, Izola and Piran, about 1,850 ha. Malvazija is the white and Refošk the red, along with Cabernet, Merlot and the local Muškat. The large Vinakoper cooperative and family wineries such as Santomas, Rojac, Korenika & Moškon and Pucer z Vrha make most of the wine.","producers":["Santomas","Rojac","Korenika & Moškon","Vinakoper","Pucer z Vrha"],"rslug":"primorska"},"si-stajerska-slovenija":{"name":"Štajerska Slovenija","cat":"ZGP","region":"Podravje","created":"EU PDO 2009","area_ha":5400,"styles":["white","sweet","sparkling"],"grapes":"Laški rizling, Šipon, Sauvignon, Renski rizling, Sivi pinot, Traminec, Muškat, Kerner, Ranina","summary":"Štajerska Slovenija is the largest Slovenian district, about 5,400 ha across the steep hills of Slovenian Styria from Maribor and Ptuj to Ljutomer-Ormož, Haloze and Slovenske gorice. It shares its style with Austria's Südsteiermark across the border: racy, aromatic whites from Sauvignon Blanc, Laški rizling, Šipon (Furmint), Renski rizling, Sivi pinot, Traminec, Muškat and Kerner, often grown on terraces at 30 degrees or more, plus late-harvest, botrytis and ice wines. Jeruzalem in Ljutomer-Ormož and the Haloze hills near Ptuj are the classic sites; producers include Puklavec, Verus, Steyer, Gaube, Kogl, Valdhuber, Heaps Good Wine and the old cooperatives Ptujska klet and Vinag.","terroir":"Marl, sandstone and clay on steep terraced hills; continental climate with long, cool autumns.","producers":["Puklavec","Verus","Steyer","Kogl","Valdhuber","Ptujska klet","Gaube","Dveri-Pax"],"nerd_note":"Dveri-Pax is the wine estate of Admont Abbey in Austria, whose Benedictines held vineyards near Jarenina from the 12th century.","rslug":"podravje"},"si-teran":{"name":"Teran","cat":"PTP","region":"Primorska","created":"EU PDO 2006","styles":["red"],"grapes":"Refošk (100%)","summary":"Teran is a recognised traditional designation (PTP) and EU PDO for red wine made 100% from Refošk on the terra rossa of the Kras. The iron-rich soil gives a deep purple wine with very high acidity, sour cherry and blackberry fruit and a reputation in local folk medicine for being good for the blood. Traditionally it is drunk young with Karst prosciutto (*pršut*). Croatian Istria also uses the name Teran for a related but distinct grape; a 2017 EU derogation allowing Croatian producers to put Teran on labels alongside 'Hrvatska Istra' was contested by Slovenia in the EU courts.","terroir":"Terra rossa over limestone on the Karst plateau.","producers":["Čotar","Vinakras","Renčel","Lisjak"],"nerd_note":"Teran's maximum yield (90 hl/ha) is higher than other Slovenian PDOs because Refošk on the Karst crops modestly anyway; its high natural acidity is the defining analytical trait.","rslug":"primorska"},"si-vipavska-dolina":{"name":"Vipavska dolina","cat":"ZGP","region":"Primorska","created":"EU PDO 2006","area_ha":2100,"styles":["white","orange","red"],"grapes":"Zelen, Pinela, Rebula, Malvazija, Laški rizling, Sauvignon, Chardonnay; Merlot, Barbera, Refošk","summary":"The Vipava valley runs west from the Nanos plateau towards Gorizia, a corridor where the bora wind blows hard enough to tip lorries; growers build stone walls and plant trees as windbreaks. About 2,100 ha on flysch slopes make fresh and macerated whites from Rebula, Malvazija, Laški rizling, Sauvignon and the two natives, Zelen (herbal, gooseberry-like) and Pinela (light and nervy), plus reds from Merlot, Barbera and Refošk. Batič, Mlečnik, Guerila, Burja, Sutor, Tilia and Lepa Vida are among the leading estates.","terroir":"Flysch and marl on the valley sides, alluvium on the floor; sub-Mediterranean climate swept by the bora, which keeps vines dry and healthy.","producers":["Batič","Mlečnik","Burja","Guerila","Sutor","Tilia","Lepa Vida","Fon"],"nerd_note":"Zelen and Pinela were nearly extinct in the 1980s; Vipava growers rebuilt them from a few old vineyards, and both are now protected local specialities.","rslug":"primorska"}}};
